<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>How to Embrace Suffering | Feels Like Om</title>
    <meta name="description" content="How to Embrace Suffering — a seven-day silent retreat in West Sikkim with Buddhist philosophy, meditation and four days of noble silence." />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/type-system.css" />
  </head>

  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand" href="/">Feels Like Om</a>
      <nav class="main-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary>ABOUT</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/about/our-story">Our story</a>
            <a href="/about/getting-to-sikkim">Getting to Sikkim</a>
            <a href="/about/visa-and-permits">Visa and permits</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="nav-dropdown">
          <summary class="active">JOURNEYS</summary>
          <div class="submenu">
            <a href="/journeys/the-flagship">The Flagship</a>
            <a href="/journeys/how-to-embrace-suffering" aria-current="page">How to Embrace Suffering</a>
            <a href="/journeys#feels-like-home">Feels Like Home</a>
            <a href="/journeys#way-of-the-yaks">Way of the Yaks</a>
          </div>
        </details>
        <a href="/reflections">REFLECTIONS</a>
        <a href="/contact">CONTACT</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="How to Embrace Suffering page sections">
      <a href="#intentions"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Intentions</span></a>
      <a href="#who"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Who it’s for</span></a>
      <a href="#teacher"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Teacher</span></a>
      <a href="#journey"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Itinerary</span></a>
      <a href="#stay-longer"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Stay longer</span></a>
      <a href="#details"><span class="section-nav-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="section-nav-label">Details</span></a>
    </nav>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">West Sikkim | Silent retreat | Buddhist Philosophy</p>
          <h1>How to Embrace Suffering</h1>
          <p class="hero-line">To be free.</p>
          <div class="hero-meta" aria-label="Retreat information">
            <p><strong>Group size:</strong> 2–6</p>
            <p><strong>Date:</strong> Nov 5–11 2026</p>
            <p><strong>Closing date:</strong> 1 October</p>
          </div>
          <a class="button hero-cta" href="/contact">Enquire about the retreat</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="opening-quote" aria-label="Opening reflection">
        <blockquote>
          “The answers to peace are all within us, otherwise we keep looking outwards.”
          <cite>— Tshampo</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </section>

      <section id="intentions" class="program-intro" aria-label="Retreat intentions">
        <div class="program-intro-inner">
          <div class="program-images" aria-label="Retreat image placeholders">
            <div class="image-placeholder program-image program-image-large"><span>Meditation / monastery photograph</span></div>
            <div class="image-placeholder program-image program-image-small"><span>West Sikkim photograph</span></div>
          </div>

          <div class="intent-copy intent-left">
            <p>This silent retreat is</p>
            <p>Less about what you can <em>gain</em></p>
            <p>More about what you can <em>let go of</em></p>
          </div>

          <div class="intent-copy intent-right">
            <p>You’re not a self-improvement project.</p>
            <p>We’re not measuring “progress”.</p>
            <p>We’re creating a supportive space for you to</p>
            <p>slow down</p>
            <p>notice what’s going on within and around you</p>
            <p>then you decide what to let go of</p>
            <p>and how to go forward.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="intent-copy intent-center">
            <p>Join us in letting go of what’s heavy,</p>
            <p>embody the soul-expanding power of</p>
            <p>being alive,</p>
            <p>by being in the</p>
            <p class="present-word">present</p>
            <p>moment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="who" class="section who-section" aria-labelledby="who-title">
        <div class="wide">
          <h2 id="who-title">Who is this for?</h2>
          <div class="who-summary">
            <p>Curious, but apprehensive</p>
            <p>In a liminal period</p>
            <p>Feeling called to meditate with Sikkim’s living energy</p>
          </div>

          <div class="audience-grid">
            <article>
              <span>01</span>
              <h3>Curious, but apprehensive</h3>
              <p>You’ve been curious about meditation, but the 10-day long silent retreats feel like a huge commitment.</p>
              <p>Ten days of no talking, no phone, just meditation. It can feel intimidating, especially for first timers.</p>
              <p>Part of you wants to try, but you might also be thinking “I’m not sure I can do that.”</p>
              <p>This retreat could be a stepping stone for you.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>02</span>
              <h3>In a liminal period</h3>
              <p>The word “liminal” comes from the Latin word <em>limen</em>, which means threshold. To be in a liminal space means to be on the precipice of something new but not quite there yet. <a href="https://www.verywellmind.com/the-impact-of-liminal-space-on-your-mental-health-5204371">Read more about liminal space.</a></p>
              <p>Maybe you feel stuck, experienced deep loss that made you confront impermanence, or consistently feel the ache of restlessness.</p>
              <p>Give yourself permission to step out of the container that can no longer contain who you might be becoming.</p>
              <p>Step into a space to slow down, explore who you are, and what you really want.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>03</span>
              <h3>Feeling called to meditate with Sikkim’s living energy</h3>
              <p>Perhaps you already have a meditation practice, and you’ve felt that where we practise matters.</p>
              <p>Every place has its own energy. People who have come here before say they felt a different kind of energy in Sikkim.</p>
              <p>According to Tibetan Buddhist tradition, Sikkim is considered a hidden land, a <em>beyul</em>, chosen and blessed by Guru Padmasambhava. It’s believed that meditating here multiplies the merit, <em>for you and all beings.</em></p>
              <p>Walk among the trees. Talk to the river. Meditate with the mountains.</p>
              <p>Come and experience it for yourself, and decide what you feel.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="teacher" class="teacher-section">
        <div class="teacher-media image-placeholder tall"><span>Portrait of Tshampo-la</span></div>
        <div class="teacher-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow dark">Your meditation teacher</p>
          <h2>Acharya Jigme Wongchuk Bhutia <span>(Tshampo-la)</span></h2>
          <blockquote>“Three years, three months, and three weeks.”</blockquote>
          <p>That’s how long Tshampo-la sat in a silent retreat for.</p>
          <p>Despite understanding the Buddhist teachings on a deep theoretical level after twelve years of institutional training, he still felt something missing.</p>
          <p>So he entered silence for three years, three months, and three weeks.</p>
          <p>After the retreat, Tshampo-la understood that the inner peace we’re searching for is all within us. “Meditation makes me feel so free. The answers to peace are all within us, otherwise we keep looking outwards.”</p>
          <p class="teacher-pull">Book wisdom is so different from lived wisdom.</p>
          <p>Since the retreat, Tshampo-la has been teaching across Sikkim and internationally. He holds weekly meditation and Dharma talks for the villagers, teaches the young ones in monastic school, and has conducted Dharma teachings in Taiwan and Hong Kong.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="journey" class="section rhythm" aria-labelledby="journey-title">
        <div class="wide">
          <div class="journey-intro">
            <h2 id="journey-title">The seven-day journey</h2>
            <p>This residential retreat will be held entirely in English.</p>
            <p>The modes of learning include:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Noble silence for four days</li>
              <li>Guided and silent meditation sessions</li>
              <li>Group discussions and reflections outside periods of noble silence</li>
              <li>Daily Dharma talks with Tshampo-la</li>
              <li>Personalised 1-1 sessions with Tshampo-la</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Because the group is limited to six meditators, there is more time for personal guidance, questions and 1-1 conversations.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="days-grid retreat-days">
            <article>
              <span>Day 1</span>
              <h3>Arrival and welcome</h3>
              <div class="day-detail">
                <p>Arrive at Bagdogra Airport</p>
                <p>Private transportation to accommodation</p>
                <p>Welcome dinner &amp; retreat orientation</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>Days 2–5</span>
              <h3>Being present in noble silence</h3>
              <div class="day-detail day-detail-long">
                <p>For four days, we enter noble silence.</p>
                <p>This means divorcing our phones and stepping away from ordinary conversations, so that your attention can be dedicated to your practice.</p>
                <p>A day may look like:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Morning meditation (sitting, then walking)</li>
                  <li>Breakfast</li>
                  <li>Dharma talk</li>
                  <li>Group meditation in monastery</li>
                  <li>Lunch</li>
                  <li>Rest / 1-1 sessions with Tshampo</li>
                  <li>Afternoon meditation</li>
                  <li>Dharma talk</li>
                  <li>Dinner</li>
                  <li>Metta meditation &amp; dedication</li>
                  <li>Group discussions and reflections</li>
                </ul>
                <p>Tshampo-la said we always have to end the day with Metta meditation &amp; dedication.</p>
                <p>We dedicate the merits of our collective practice to all beings:</p>
                <p><em>May I be free from suffering.</em><br /><em>May all beings be free from suffering.</em></p>
                <p>Themes covered include:</p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Introduction to Buddhist philosophy</li>
                  <li>Gratitude, a practice</li>
                  <li>Precious human life</li>
                  <li>Karma, everything is connected</li>
                  <li>Impermanence</li>
                  <li>Attachment</li>
                  <li>Ego and suffering</li>
                </ul>
                <p>These themes supplement the meditation sessions.</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>Day 6</span>
              <h3>Gratitude and Metta Day</h3>
              <div class="day-detail">
                <p>Tshampo-la has invited us to his village, and to visit the monastery where he practises.</p>
                <p>We will hold a gratitude and metta ceremony, to share the merits of our collective practice with all beings.</p>
                <p>A closing dinner to celebrate the connections you’ve made over the past week.</p>
                <p>And to celebrate you.</p>
              </div>
            </article>

            <article>
              <span>Day 7</span>
              <h3>Not Goodbye</h3>
              <div class="day-detail">
                <p>In Sikkim, instead of goodbye, we say <em>pheri bhetum</em>, may we meet again :-)</p>
                <p>You may choose to depart or extend your stay.</p>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="stay-longer" class="section stay-longer">
        <div class="wide split-section">
          <div class="copy-block">
            <h2>Stay longer</h2>
            <p>If you choose to extend your stay, there is the option to add-on Feels Like Om field immersion activities.</p>
            <p>With the intention of learning from nature and its people, these aren’t sightseeing activities, but immersive hands-on learning experiences.</p>
            <p>A sample of the activities can be found here.</p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/journeys/the-flagship">Explore the field immersion →</a>
          </div>
          <div class="image-stack">
            <div class="image-placeholder"><span>Field immersion photograph</span></div>
            <div class="image-placeholder"><span>Community activity photograph</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="details" class="section details-section" aria-labelledby="details-title">
        <div class="wide">
          <h2 id="details-title">Details</h2>
          <div class="details-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Retreat costs</h3>
              <p>To support retreat costs, we ask for S$___ per person.</p>
              <p>This covers your accommodation and vegetarian meals, retreat logistics, and ceremony-related costs.</p>
              <p>Airport transfers to and from Bagdogra are <strong>not</strong> included, but can be arranged for you, and are paid directly to your driver.</p>
              <p>Flights, travel insurance, visas, and personal expenses are also not included.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Accommodation</h3>
              <p>You’ll have a private room with an attached bathroom. Hot water is available.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Dana</h3>
              <p>Dharma teachings and guided meditation sessions are offered compassionately, without a fee.</p>
              <p>If you wish, you may offer dana (voluntary donation) to Tshampo-la in person at any point of the retreat. Dana is entirely voluntary.</p>
            </article>

            <article>
              <h3>Supporting Feels Like Om</h3>
              <p>Feels Like Om’s work extends beyond this retreat and the other field immersion programs we host.</p>
              <p>We are working towards building a third space in the village. A room where:</p>
              <ul>
                <li>Children can be children</li>
                <li>Futures can be imagined and co-created</li>
                <li>Small-scale collaborations in art, culture, music, science, learning, and brainstorming community events can happen for the villagers</li>
              </ul>
              <p>If you would like to support this work, we’ll be very grateful for your help. Again, there is no expectation to do so.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <div class="details-cta">
            <a class="button" href="/contact">Enquire about How to Embrace Suffering →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section other-journeys">
        <div class="narrow center">
          <h2>Other journeys</h2>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script>
      const sectionNav = document.querySelector('.section-nav');
      const hero = document.querySelector('.hero');

      const updateSectionNav = () => {
        if (!sectionNav || !hero) return;
        sectionNav.classList.toggle('is-visible', hero.getBoundingClientRect().bottom <= 0);
      };

      updateSectionNav();
      window.addEventListener('scroll', updateSectionNav, { passive: true });
      window.addEventListener('resize', updateSectionNav);
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(*) { box-sizing: border-box; }
  :global(html) { scroll-behavior: smooth; scroll-padding-top: 2rem; }
  body { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-body); background: #f4efe5; color: #18301f; }
  p { line-height: 1.75; }
  a { color: inherit; }

  .site-header { position:absolute; top:0; left:0; right:0; z-index:50; display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:2rem; padding:1.5rem 4%; color:#f4efe5; }
  .brand { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; }
  .main-nav { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:1.5rem; letter-spacing:.08em; }
  .main-nav > a,.main-nav summary { color:inherit; text-decoration:none; cursor:pointer; }
  .main-nav .active { border-bottom:1px solid currentColor; }
  .nav-dropdown { position:relative; }
  .nav-dropdown summary { list-style:none; }
  .nav-dropdown summary::-webkit-details-marker { display:none; }
  .submenu { position:absolute; top:calc(100% + .65rem); right:0; width:max-content; min-width:13rem; padding:.7rem; background:rgba(244,239,229,.98); box-shadow:0 12px 30px rgba(8,20,12,.14); opacity:0; visibility:hidden; transform:translateY(-4px); transition:opacity 160ms ease,visibility 160ms ease,transform 160ms ease; z-index:60; }
  .submenu::before { content:""; position:absolute; top:-.75rem; left:0; right:0; height:.75rem; }
  .submenu a { display:block; padding:.65rem .75rem; color:#18301f; text-decoration:none; letter-spacing:0; }
  .submenu a:hover { background:rgba(24,48,31,.06); }
  @media (hover:hover) and (pointer:fine) {
    .nav-dropdown .submenu { pointer-events:none; }
    .nav-dropdown:hover .submenu { opacity:1; visibility:visible; transform:translateY(0); pointer-events:auto; }
    .nav-dropdown:not(:hover) .submenu { opacity:0; visibility:hidden; transform:translateY(-4px); }
  }

  .section-nav { position:fixed; top:50%; right:1.15rem; z-index:40; width:42px; padding:.4rem .25rem; display:grid; gap:.1rem; background:transparent; transform:translateY(-50%); overflow:hidden; opacity:0; visibility:hidden; pointer-events:none; transition:width 240ms ease,opacity 220ms ease,visibility 220ms ease; }
